<https://example.org/dmo/id/complication/diabetic-ketoacidosis> a dmo:Complication ;
    rdfs:label "Diabetic ketoacidosis" ;
    dmo:affectedOrgan "Systemic" ;
    dmo:complicationCode "diabetic-ketoacidosis" ;
    dmo:definition "The management of diabetic ketoacidosis in adults" ;
    dmo:isEmergency "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    dmo:mondoCode "MONDO:0005041" ;
    dmo:name "Diabetic ketoacidosis" ;
    dmo:onsetPattern "Acute" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The management of diabetic ketoacidosis in adults" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Delayed commencement leading to insufficient time to minimise neonatal hypoglycaemia and/or diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "or has urinary ketones ++ or more, or high ketones (>1.5 mmol/L)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Intrinsic complications including user errors with establishment and cessation leading to DKA, fluid and electrolyte imbalance and inadvertent hypoglycaemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Diabetic ketoacidosis is a medical emergency requiring prompt treatment, and is different to a ketosis of pregnancy. Women who are suspected of having DKA are admitted to the delivery suite or the high dependency unit where they can receive medical and obstetric care." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "DKA in pregnancy should be managed in critical care" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The goals of treatment include: 1. Initial fluid resuscitation 2. Administration of FRIII to stop the ketogenesis 3. Administration of potassium 4. Prevention of hypoglycaemia from use of the FRIII 5. Control of BP 6. Prevention of fluid overload 7. Timely delivery 8. Monitoring to avoid the complications of PET" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "This will usually be associated with a rapid deterioration in maternal glycaemic control and even precipitation of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

