<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/add-10-dextrose-to-run-alongside-0-9-nacl-when-capillary-glucose-14-mmol-l> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Add 10% dextrose to run alongside 0.9% NaCl when capillary glucose < 14 mmol/L" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "add-10-dextrose-to-run-alongside-0-9-nacl-when-capillary-glucose-14-mmol-l" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Add 10% dextrose to run alongside 0.9% NaCl when capillary glucose < 14 mmol/L. Initially this should be administered at a rate of 50 mL/h but rate of infusion may need to be adjusted to prevent hypoglycaemia and avoid fluid overload or hyponatraemia" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Add 10% dextrose to run alongside 0.9% NaCl when capillary glucose < 14 mmol/L. Initially this should be administered at a rate of 50 mL/h but rate of infusion may need to be adjusted to prevent hypoglycaemia and avoid fluid overload or hyponatraemia" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/add-40-mmol-of-kcl-l-of-normal-saline-from-the-2nd-litre-of-fluids-onward> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Add 40 mmol of KCL/L of normal saline from the 2nd litre of fluids onward" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "add-40-mmol-of-kcl-l-of-normal-saline-from-the-2nd-litre-of-fluids-onward" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Potassium may not be needed in the first bag. Aim for keeping K+ between 4.0 and 5.5 mmol/L. Add 40 mmol of KCL/L of normal saline from the 2nd litre of fluids onward. Use the pre-prepared 0.3% KCl with 0.9% NaCl" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Potassium may not be needed in the first bag. Aim for keeping K+ between 4.0 and 5.5 mmol/L. Add 40 mmol of KCL/L of normal saline from the 2nd litre of fluids onward. Use the pre-prepared 0.3% KCl with 0.9% NaCl" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/additional-capillary-glucose-tests-during-labour-and-delivery-for-women-using-cgm> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Additional capillary glucose tests during labour and delivery for women using CGM" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Women using intermittent or real time continuous glucose monitoring (CGM)" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "additional-capillary-glucose-tests-during-labour-and-delivery-for-women-using-cgm" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Women using intermittent or real time continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) should be advised that additional capillary glucose tests may be required during labour and delivery. CGM measures interstitial glucose levels, and changes may lag 5 - 10 minutes behind capillary blood glucose measurements. CGM can be used to guide diabetes self-management but CGM should NOT BE USED to guide VRIII doses" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Women using intermittent or real time continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) should be advised that additional capillary glucose tests may be required during labour and delivery. CGM measures interstitial glucose levels, and changes may lag 5 - 10 minutes behind capillary blood glucose measurements. CGM can be used to guide diabetes self-management but CGM should NOT BE USED to guide VRIII doses" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/adequate-supply-of-insulin-syringes-and-subcutaneous-needs-on-obstetric-wards> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Adequate supply of insulin syringes and subcutaneous needs on obstetric wards" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
