<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/postpartum-carbohydrate-intake-for-breastfeeding-women> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Postpartum carbohydrate intake for breastfeeding women" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Women who are breastfeeding or expressing" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "postpartum-carbohydrate-intake-for-breastfeeding-women" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Thereafter, healthy eating should be encouraged with increased carbohydrate as required to minimise the risk of hypoglycaemia, if breastfeeding / expressing. Women should be advised to snack (10 - 15 g carbohydrate) and drink each time they feed or express milk (including night feeds). Up to 450 extra calories per day may be needed when feeding is fully established" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Thereafter, healthy eating should be encouraged with increased carbohydrate as required to minimise the risk of hypoglycaemia, if breastfeeding / expressing. Women should be advised to snack (10 - 15 g carbohydrate) and drink each time they feed or express milk (including night feeds). Up to 450 extra calories per day may be needed when feeding is fully established" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/postpartum-glucose-monitoring-for-women-with-gestational-diabetes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Postpartum glucose monitoring for women with gestational diabetes" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Women with gestational diabetes (GDM)" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "postpartum-glucose-monitoring-for-women-with-gestational-diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "In women with gestational diabetes (GDM), all glucose lowering medications should be stopped after the placenta is delivered. Glucose levels should be monitored pre- and post-meals for 24 hours to detect new or pre-existing diabetes (fasting glucose >7.0 mmol/L and post-meal >11.1 mmol/L)" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "In women with gestational diabetes (GDM), all glucose lowering medications should be stopped after the placenta is delivered. Glucose levels should be monitored pre- and post-meals for 24 hours to detect new or pre-existing diabetes (fasting glucose >7.0 mmol/L and post-meal >11.1 mmol/L)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/postpartum-glucose-target-range-for-women-on-oral-medications-before-pregnancy> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Postpartum glucose target range for women on oral medications before pregnancy" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Women on oral medications before pregnancy" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "postpartum-glucose-target-range-for-women-on-oral-medications-before-pregnancy" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Because metformin does not cause hypoglycaemia, a target glucose range of 4.0 - 10.0 mmol/L is acceptable. For those on other oral glucose lowering medications the target range is 6.0 - 10.0 mmol/L" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Because metformin does not cause hypoglycaemia, a target glucose range of 4.0 - 10.0 mmol/L is acceptable. For those on other oral glucose lowering medications the target range is 6.0 - 10.0 mmol/L" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

