<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/postpartum-insulin-dose-reduction-for-women-with-insulin-treated-diabetes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Postpartum insulin dose reduction for women with insulin-treated diabetes" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Women with insulin-treated diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "postpartum-insulin-dose-reduction-for-women-with-insulin-treated-diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Insulin requirements drop immediately after delivery of the placenta. Commonly used options include reverting to the pre-pregnancy dose, 25% reduction from the first trimester dose or 50% of the late pregnancy doses" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Insulin requirements drop immediately after delivery of the placenta. Commonly used options include reverting to the pre-pregnancy dose, 25% reduction from the first trimester dose or 50% of the late pregnancy doses" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/postpartum-insulin-dose-review-for-women-with-insulin-treated-diabetes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Postpartum insulin dose review for women with insulin-treated diabetes" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Women with insulin-treated diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "postpartum-insulin-dose-review-for-women-with-insulin-treated-diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Postpartum insulin doses should be reviewed in conjunction with diabetes team daily, with an emphasis on minimising risk of maternal hypoglycaemia, and before hospital discharge" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Postpartum insulin doses should be reviewed in conjunction with diabetes team daily, with an emphasis on minimising risk of maternal hypoglycaemia, and before hospital discharge" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/postpartum-insulin-pump-setting-change-for-women-on-insulin-pump> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Postpartum insulin pump setting change for women on insulin pump" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Women on insulin pump" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "postpartum-insulin-pump-setting-change-for-women-on-insulin-pump" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "If she hasn’t already done so, the woman must change the pump settings to her postnatal settings as described on her individual care plan provided by the diabetes team. If the woman’s pump has been discontinued it should be re-connected for one hour prior to discontinuing the VRIII. Only discontinue VRIII when the woman can safely manage her own pump" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If she hasn’t already done so, the woman must change the pump settings to her postnatal settings as described on her individual care plan provided by the diabetes team. If the woman’s pump has been discontinued it should be re-connected for one hour prior to discontinuing the VRIII. Only discontinue VRIII when the woman can safely manage her own pump" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/postpartum-insulin-regimen-resumption-for-women-with-insulin-treated-diabetes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Postpartum insulin regimen resumption for women with insulin-treated diabetes" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Women with insulin-treated diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "postpartum-insulin-regimen-resumption-for-women-with-insulin-treated-diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Postpartum insulin regimen should be resumed as per individual diabetes management plan. If there is no documented diabetes plan, the early pregnancy (about 12 weeks gestation) doses should be reduced by 25% or the late pregnancy (about 36 weeks gestation) doses by at least 50%" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Postpartum insulin regimen should be resumed as per individual diabetes management plan. If there is no documented diabetes plan, the early pregnancy (about 12 weeks gestation) doses should be reduced by 25% or the late pregnancy (about 36 weeks gestation) doses by at least 50%" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

