<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/start-vriii-to-achieve-target-blood-glucose-of-4-0-7-8-or-5-0-8-0-mmol-l> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Start VRIII to achieve target blood glucose of 4.0 – 7.8 or 5.0 – 8.0 mmol/L" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Women on diet control/oral treatment and/or single or multiple dose insulin therapy receiving antenatal steroids" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "start-vriii-to-achieve-target-blood-glucose-of-4-0-7-8-or-5-0-8-0-mmol-l" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Start variable rate intravenous insulin infusion (VRIII) (50 units human soluble insulin [Humulin® S or Actrapid®] made up to 50 mL with 0.9% NaCl) to achieve the target blood glucose of either 4.0 – 7.8 or 5.0 – 8.0 mmol/L. Use the scale in Tables 6 and 7 below." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Start variable rate intravenous insulin infusion (VRIII) (50 units human soluble insulin [Humulin® S or Actrapid®] made up to 50 mL with 0.9% NaCl) to achieve the target blood glucose of either 4.0 – 7.8 or 5.0 – 8.0 mmol/L. Use the scale in Tables 6 and 7 below." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/start-with-1l-0-9-nacl-over-60-minutes-and-continue-with-hydration-fluids-as-per-clinical-need> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Start with 1L 0.9% NaCl over 60 minutes and continue with hydration fluids as per clinical need" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "start-with-1l-0-9-nacl-over-60-minutes-and-continue-with-hydration-fluids-as-per-clinical-need" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "The fluid requirement may be lower in pregnancy. Start with 1L 0.9% NaCl over 60 minutes and continue with the hydration fluids as per clinical need. Often patients with severe dehydration and typical DKA would need 1 litre of normal saline each in subsequent 2 hour, 2 hour, 4 hour, 4 hour, and 6 hours after the first bag" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The fluid requirement may be lower in pregnancy. Start with 1L 0.9% NaCl over 60 minutes and continue with the hydration fluids as per clinical need. Often patients with severe dehydration and typical DKA would need 1 litre of normal saline each in subsequent 2 hour, 2 hour, 4 hour, 4 hour, and 6 hours after the first bag" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds_12_managing_diabetes_and_hyperglycaemia_during_labour_and_birth_with_qr_code_february_2023> .

